    <body>
      <div type="clause" n="1.1">
        <head><ref type="lawCode" target="law:VIAtr">VI Atr</ref> 1.1</head>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="la" source="#liebermann" n="1.1"><pb n="246" ed="#liebermann"/>[Not in D]</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="1.1" corresp="#wit-k"><pb n="246" ed="#liebermann"/>⁊ anum cynehlaforde holdlice hyran ⁊ georne hine healdan mid rihtan getrywðan.</ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="ang" source="#robertson" n="1[b]" corresp="#wit-k"><pb n="90" ed="#robertson"/>⁊ anum cynehlaforde holdlice hyran ⁊ georne hine healdan mid rihtan getrywðan.</ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="ang" source="#rabin-doml" corresp="#wit-k"><pb n="160" ed="#rabin-doml"/>and anum cynehlaforde holdlice hyran and georne hine healdan mid rihtan getrywðan.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="de" source="#liebermann"><pb n="246" ed="#liebermann"/>und Einem königlichen Herrn getreu gehorchen und mit rechter Treue<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="1" target="#VIAtr_1-1.lnote.de.1"/> willig an ihm festhalten.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude" ana="#fromGerman">and loyally obey one royal lord and willingly hold to him with true fidelity.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#robertson" corresp="#wit-k"><pb n="91" ed="#robertson"/>and loyally obey one royal lord, and readily support him with due fidelity<ptr type="editorNote" n="4" target="#VIAtr_1-1.robnote.n.4"/>.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#rabin-doml" corresp="#wit-k"><pb n="161" ed="#rabin-doml"/>and loyally obey one royal lord, and willingly follow him with proper devotion.</ab>
        <note type="comparison" source="#liebermann" n="246"><ref target="clause:VAtr_1">V Atr 1</ref>; <ref target="clause:VAtr_35">V Atr 35</ref></note>
        <note type="comparisonPrinted" source="#liebermann">ebd. 1. 35</note>
        <note type="comparedBy" source="#liebermann"><ref target="clause:VIIIAtr_44-1">VIII Atr 44.1</ref>; <ref target="clause:ICn_1">I Cn 1</ref></note>
        <note type="comparedBy" source="#kennedy" n="59"><ref target="clause:Cn-1018_part-002">Cn 1018 1</ref></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="VIAtr_1-1.lnote.de.1" n="1" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">175</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">1</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">Plural sing. Bed.</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">Plural with singular meaning</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="VIAtr_1-1.lnote.de.a" n="a" source="#liebermann-erkl" rend="wholeClause"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">175</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">1</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">Unbetontes <hi rend="italic">e</hi> schreibt der Paraphrast auch sonst <hi rend="italic">ę</hi>: <hi rend="italic">subponeręnt</hi> 2; <hi rend="italic">defuęrit</hi> 4; <hi rend="italic">sobrię</hi> 1, 3; <hi rend="italic">castę</hi> Adverbien 5</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">The paraphrast writes unstressed <hi rend="italic">e</hi> as <hi rend="italic">ę</hi> elsewhere too: <hi rend="italic">subponeręnt</hi> 2; <hi rend="italic">defuęrit</hi> 4; <hi rend="italic">sobrię</hi> 1, 3; <hi rend="italic">castę</hi> adverbs 5</seg></note>
        <note type="editorNote" subtype="endnote" xml:id="VIAtr_1-1.robnote.n.4" n="4" source="#robertson"><bibl><biblScope unit="page">342</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="en">The Latin paraphrase adds in explanation: [<hi rend="italic">plebs</hi>] <hi rend="italic">paganorum incursionibus vel inruptionibus ceterisque calamitatum erumnis pluriformium obprimentibus, a religionis tramite recto anfractibus errabundis exorbitans.</hi></seg></note>
      </div>
    </body>
